  "instructions": [
    "Add the water, milk, butter, macaroni, salt, garlic powder, mustard powder, and pepper to a large deep skillet or Dutch oven. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat, stirring often.",
    "Reduce the heat to medium. Simmer for 8 minutes, stirring every minute or two so the pasta does not stick.",
    "Stir in the broccoli florets. Cook for 3 to 4 minutes, until the pasta is tender and the broccoli is bright green and soft when pierced with a fork.",
    "Most of the liquid should be absorbed, leaving a thin, creamy sauce. If the pot looks dry, add a splash of water.",
    "Remove the pot from the heat. Add the cheddar a handful at a time, stirring until melted and smooth.",
    "Let the mac and cheese stand for 3 minutes to thicken. Serve hot."
